**I withdraw my proposed audit:** your reading is right, and a blinded control for gate 1 is the better next step—but its result cannot prove that *any* writer can or cannot pass.

1. **The audit is largely done.** The 11-article comparison already examined carried versus empty starts, and the fortnight trace followed the company figures through to the judges. The latter found five relevant undelivered statements on three questions, with neither reader predicting an answer change. The DOJ/FTC and equity-commitment cases remain uncertain, but I cannot point to an unexamined shared mechanism that makes another broad audit the best next decision. The studies are small, so “closed” means closed as a next repair route, not proven absent in production. [Carried-library result](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/carried-library/RESULT.md), [delivery trace](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-trace/RESULT.md)

2. **Yes: measure the reading method next, with a narrower decision rule.** The existing repeat showed the same gate verdict twice, but not whether its marks were correct; five of six controls were read as expected. A blinded comparison with independently written answers can investigate that missing validity question. [Repeated reading](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/gate1-stick/RESULT.md)

   The proposed test needs these corrections:

   - **Twenty reference answers cannot establish a 2% fault rate.** One fault is 5%; zero faults still leaves substantial uncertainty. Topics and repeated sends are clustered, so they cannot be treated as 131 independent trials.
   - **A reference fault does not prove the gate impossible.** The writer may have made a real mistake. Conversely, agreement between model families can reflect a shared misreading. Each settled fault needs an independent source-and-rule review, with genuine answer errors separated from reader errors and unresolved cases.
   - **Prevent leakage and cherry-picking.** Fix the outside-44 topic selection and stored input packets before writing; include the different question and refusal types. Writers must not see stored answers, previous marks or one another’s work. Blind references and frozen answers together, including author and order; include known wrong and sound controls. Reader-family overlap remains a limitation.
   - **Use the full gate accounting.** Include line 2 and the topic-level lines as well as 1, 3 and 4; otherwise a writer could look strong by refusing difficult questions or omitting parts. Pass each reference through the same schema, code checks and rendered packet as the frozen answers.
   - **Do not promise another test on the 44.** D426 explicitly says no fifth Stage A and no further tuning on them. A new version can be opened by council under D439, but a later measurement needs its own decision consistent with that stop. [D426](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS.md:770)

   **Decision-moving result:** a confirmed reader error on a sound reference, or a clear, repeated difference favouring sound references on the same topics, identifies whether the next investigation should address reading validity or step design. **Close this control:** the sample yields no independently confirmed reader error and no interpretable difference; report its uncertainty rather than declaring the gate reachable or unreachable. Subscription sessions have no API charge, but their time and any actual charges should still be recorded.

**CONSENSUS: Run the blinded outside-44 reference control at $0 in API spending, with the safeguards and narrower conclusions above; leave the gate and D426 unchanged.**
